    text: "TDD evidence: a failing regression was recorded before the implementation path was changed. The connected recovery suite now passes nine tests across five files, covering exact preview refusal, legacy redaction consistency and tamper refusal, legacy omitted scalars, immutable acceptance backfill, root/inherited reservation parity, and actual Git rebase abort. Repository-wide gates and hosted review are still pending."
  - created_at: "2026-09-06T05:12:53.441Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Reproduction refinement: the historical 2026.9.4 writer uses requested_preference and clone_local, not only the preferred-era shape. A real temporary Git repository reproduces schema_invalid collections at decisions[0] when writeMergeReceipt receives an undefined base scalar: JSON serialization omits the property. The current driver encodes missing scalars, but the writer boundary itself still permits this loss. Extend the regression and writer normalization to preserve all scalar slots, and accept identified older clone-local receipts with omitted non-selected slots. This is a reproducible compatibility defect; the private GH-1201 receipt remains unavailable, so its exact malformed coordinate is not asserted."
  - created_at: "2026-09-06T05:27:21.507Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Writer and legacy reader regression now passes: all five undefined scalar slots survive JSON storage; a prior requested_preference/clone_local receipt with an omitted base remains byte-identical during reads and settles without deleting evidence. Selected retained/discarded values remain required on historical reads. Malformed collection and operation fixtures retain fail-closed diagnostics with bounded coordinates."
  - created_at: "2026-09-06T05:42:31.206Z"
