body: "## Report and scope\n\nSource: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1201\n\nInvestigate the reported 2026.9.4 writer to 2026.9.5 reader failure and health/reconcile recovery loop. Source inspection confirms collections is a diagnostic category, not a required top-level key: it validates fields_from_theirs, union_fields, decisions and optional merged_field_hashes. Pending and reconciled receipts share this validation before state filtering. The underlying malformed field requires a privacy-safe reproduction; absence of a collections key alone is not evidence of schema incompatibility.\n\n## Reported reproduction\n\n## Summary\n\n`pm health` fails on a merge receipt that `pm` itself wrote minutes earlier under the previous patch release. The documented remediation cannot run, because the same receipt makes `pm merge reconcile` refuse to start. The only way out is to delete the evidence file by hand — the artifact the receipt system exists to preserve.\n\n## Timeline (single repository, one afternoon)\n\n1. `pm` **2026.9.4** is the installed CLI. A `git rebase` invokes the field-aware merge driver, which writes receipt `f9067de4…` with `state: \"pending\"`.\n2. The CLI is upgraded to **2026.9.5**.\n3. `pm health --check-only` now fails:\n\n```\nok: False\nfailed_because: ['merge_decisions_unreviewed:1', 'merge_receipt_evidence_invalid:1']\n```\n\n4. `pm merge report --include-reconciled --json` names it:\n\n```json\n{\"evidence_source\":\"clone_local\",\"reason\":\"schema_invalid\",\n \"validation_error\":\"collections\",\"receipt_id\":\"f9067de4-bc6c-477a-99de-c415951b2064\"}\n```\n\n5. The remediation `pm health` points at refuses to run **at all**:\n\n```\n$ pm merge reconcile --dry-run\nError: Merge reconciliation refused 1 invalid receipt evidence file(s).\n  suggested_retry: pm health --check-only --full\nEXIT=4\n```\n\n`suggested_retry` sends the operator back to the command that produced the failure, so the two commands point at each other and neither can settle the receipt.\n\n## The schema difference is not something the writer could have satisfied\n\nThe receipt store held **19** receipts. **None of the 19** has a `collections` key. Only one is rejected:\n\n| state | count | verdict |\n|---|---|---|\n| `reconciled` | 18 | accepted |\n| `pending` | 1 | `schema_invalid: collections` |\n\nSo the field is required only on the validation path taken for a pending receipt, and the writer that produced it never emits the key. Same store, same shape, opposite verdicts — the discriminator is `state`, not the data.\n\nIn 2026.9.5's `dist/cli-bundle/sdk-merge.js` the validator requires a non-null object:\n\n```js\ncollections != \"object\" || s.collections === null ? null : s\n```\n\n## Impact\n\nA repository reaches a state where:\n\n- `pm health` is red and stays red,\n- the only remediation the CLI names cannot execute,\n- and no `pm` command can settle or repair the receipt.\n\nBecause `pm health --strict-exit` is a CI step across our fleet, this is a hard stop rather than a warning. Deleting `.git/pm-merge-receipts/<id>.json` is the only recovery, which discards the retained/discarded field values the receipt was written to preserve — in this case three fields including a full `description` and an `acceptance_criteria` pair.\n\n## Expected\n\nAny of these would break the deadlock:\n\n1. A receipt missing `collections` is treated as a valid v1 receipt (the writer never wrote the key, so absence cannot mean corruption), or migrated on read.\n2. `pm merge reconcile` still runs, quarantining invalid evidence and settling the rest, rather than refusing wholesale on a single bad candidate.\n3. A supported repair command exists, so recovery is not \"delete the evidence file\".\n\nWhatever the mechanism, a receipt written by release N should not be unreadable to release N+1 with no migration.\n\n## Environment\n\n- Written by @unbrained/pm-cli **2026.9.4**, rejected by **2026.9.5**\n- Linux, Node 22; receipt store `.git/pm-merge-receipts/`, 19 receipts\n\n## Delivery boundary\n\nIntake only in PR #1204. This item remains open and unclaimed; no implementation or reproduction success is asserted. Implement through the public SDK with thin CLI adapters and executable negative controls before closing."
